# Migrations are checksummed and reviewed as text. Keeping them LF in every
# checkout means the diff a reviewer approved is byte-for-byte the text that
# runs, on Windows as well as on the Linux runner. The checksum normalises line
# endings anyway (src/catalog.ts), and the check only rejects a file that mixes
# them; this keeps the files themselves canonical so neither ever has to.
*.sql text eol=lf
# The initdb hooks are bind-mounted into the Linux container and executed
# there. A CRLF checkout on Windows turns the shebang into "bash" and the
# container exits 127 before PostgreSQL can create a single role
# (CBD117-REVIEW-002 finding 1). Keep them LF everywhere for the same reason.
local/initdb/*.sh text eol=lf
local/initdb/*.psql text eol=lf
